<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sindh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sindh is a province of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> on the lower course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus River</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karachi">Karachi</a>. It was a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus-valley-civilisation">Indus Valley Civilisation</a>, whose city of Mohenjo-daro lies there. Arab forces under Muhammad ibn al-Qasim conquered it in 711 and 712, and later it was ruled by local dynasties, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, the Talpurs and, from 1843, the British.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sindh.jpg" alt="Sindh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.irfan44 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jinnah_Mausoleum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
